   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "Van Fraassen’s aim was to develop a semantics for sentences containing non-denoting singular terms. Even if one grants atomic sentences containing non-denoting singular terms and that some attributions of vague predicates are neither true nor false, it nevertheless seems natural not to preclude that compound sentences of a certain shape containing non-denoting terms or vague predications are either true or false, e.g., sentences of the form ‘If ⟦M⟧ , then ⟦M⟧ ’. Supervaluational semantics provid",
   "md_text": "Van Fraassen’s aim was to develop a semantics for sentences containing non-denoting singular terms. Even if one grants atomic sentences containing non-denoting singular terms and that some attributions of vague predicates are neither true nor false, it nevertheless seems natural not to preclude that compound sentences of a certain shape containing non-denoting terms or vague predications are either true or false, e.g., sentences of the form ‘If ⟦M⟧ , then ⟦M⟧ ’. Supervaluational semantics provid"
